 commonly used post-transplant. Evidence notes that because both 阿卡波糖 and immunosuppressants can cause gastrointestinal adverse reactions, its use is not recommended in NODAT management [Data: Relationships (7473, 16760)]. This contraindication highlights important clinical considerations in polypharmacy settings involving transplant recipients.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Gastrointestinal side effects are a notable risk of 阿卡波糖 therapy\",\n            \"explanation\": \"肠胀气 (flatulence) is a documented adverse reaction associated with 阿卡波糖 use. This side effect arises from undigested carbohydrates reaching the colon, where they are fermented by gut bacteria, producing gas. Clinical guidance specifically cautions against using 阿卡波糖 in populations already prone to gastrointestinal disturbances, such as transplant patients on immunosuppressants [Data: Relationships (16760)]. The prevalence and severity of this adverse effect can impact patient adherence and necessitate careful patient selection and counseling during treatment initiation.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"阿卡波糖 significantly modulates key glycemic indicators\",\n            \"explanation\": \"阿卡波糖 demonstrably affects critical diabetes-related indicators, including 胰岛素水平 (insulin levels) and 餐后血糖 (postprandial blood glucose). Clinical studies indicate that 阿卡波糖 markedly reduces both postprandial hyperglycemia and the associated rise in insulin levels following meals. This dual effect contributes to improved glycemic control without increasing the risk of hypoglycemia when used as monotherapy [Data: Relationships (4634, 4636)]. These pharmacodynamic properties support its role in managing postprandial glucose excursions, particularly in early-stage or prediabetic conditions.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Food components like 没食子酸 and 绿茶粉 enhance 阿卡波糖 activity\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Certain dietary compounds, notably 没食子酸 (gallic acid) found in blueberries and cabbage, and 绿茶粉 (green tea powder), have been shown in vitro to potentiate the alpha-glucosidase inhibitory effect of 阿卡波糖. Specifically, co-administration with 绿茶粉 reduced the IC50 of 阿卡波糖 by 55.6%, indicating substantially enhanced enzymatic inhibition. These findings suggest potential synergistic benefits when 阿卡波糖 is combined with specific foods, although clinical relevance in humans requires further validation [Data: Relationships (42181, 52907)]. Such interactions underscore the importance of considering diet in diabetes pharmacotherapy.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Concurrent use with digestive enzyme preparations reduces 阿卡波糖 efficacy\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The concomitant administration of 消化酶制剂 (digestive enzyme preparations) or 消化酶类制剂 with 阿卡波糖 is discouraged because these agents may degrade or interfere with 阿卡波糖’s action in the gastrointestinal tract, thereby diminishing its therapeutic effect. Structured clinical guidance explicitly advises avoiding simultaneous use of 阿卡波糖 with digestive enzymes, intestinal adsorbents, or bile acid sequestrants like cholestyramine [Data: Relationships (43180, 52901, 52909)]. This interaction exemplifies a clinically significant drug–drug or drug–supplement interference that prescribers must manage through appropriate dosing separation or alternative regimens.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"阿卡波糖 shows minimal interaction with 二甲基硅油\",\n            \"explanation\": \"In contrast to other interacting agents, 二甲基硅油 (dimethicone)—a common anti-foaming agent used to relieve bloating—has been evaluated for potential interaction with 阿卡波糖, and no significant pharmacokinetic or pharmacodynamic interaction was found. This suggests that 二甲基硅油 may be safely co-administered to alleviate gas-related symptoms without compromising 阿卡波糖’s glucose-lowering efficacy [Data: Relationships (52893)]. This favorable interaction profile offers a practical option for managing one of 阿卡波糖’s common side effects.\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 6.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The community presents moderate-to-high clinical impact due to 阿卡波糖's central role in diabetes management, its significant drug–food interactions, contraindications in vulnerable populations, and common adverse effects affecting patient compliance.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1782121842, "model": "qwen3-max", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1420, "prompt_tokens": 6271, "total_tokens": 7691, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1280}}, "formatted_response": null, "content": "{\n    \"title\": \"阿卡波糖 and Related Therapeutic Entities\",\n    \"summary\": \"This community centers on the antidiabetic drug 阿卡波糖 (Acarbose), which is linked to multiple symptoms, diseases, indicators, food substances, and drug classes through therapeutic indications, adverse reactions, and pharmacological interactions. Key relationships include its use for 糖耐量低减 (impaired glucose tolerance), contraindication in 移植后新发糖尿病 (new-onset diabetes after transplantation), effects on 胰岛素水平 and 餐后血糖, and adverse reaction 肠胀气. Additionally, 阿卡波糖 interacts with various agents including 没食子酸, 绿茶粉, 消化酶制剂, 肠道吸附剂, and 二甲基硅油, influencing its efficacy or safety profile.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"阿卡波糖 is indicated for managing impaired glucose tolerance\",\n            \"explanation\": \"阿卡波糖 is clinically indicated for patients with 糖耐量低减 (impaired glucose tolerance), where it helps lower postprandial blood glucose levels. This indication aligns with its mechanism as an alpha-glucosidase inhibitor t